  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe status strip gains a Report door next to the Debug info door (#1696).\nIt opens a small window:\n\n- A short title field.\n- Two buttons, \"Report a bug\" and \"Request a feature\". Each opens the\n  browser on a prefilled GitHub new-issue URL: the title, the body and the\n  `bug` / `enhancement` label are already typed.\n- A \"Copy screenshot\" button. It puts a picture of the current document\n  (the CPU raster, the MCP `render_stock` path) on the clipboard. The user\n  pastes it into the issue description and GitHub uploads it.\n\nThe body embeds the Debug info report (#157), so both paths carry the same\nfields from one source. An empty document refuses the copy in words, in the\nstatus line.\n\nThe repository also gains `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/blank-issue.md` and\n`.github/config.yml`. GitHub's prefill query works only on a blank\ntemplate, not on the issue forms. The new glyph `act-report.png` comes from\nan original SVG master, `assets/ui/svg/act-report.svg`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `report_tests.rs` (new, kittest): URL encoding, the prefilled URL shape,\n  the body content, the door open/close, the typed title in the URL, the\n  empty-document refusal, and a cube that paints into the picture.\n- `structural.rs`: the door sits on the status strip; no floating window is\n  open by default (pin kept).\n- `op_icon_table.rs`: the `Report` glyph is SVG-mastered and unique.\n- `cargo xtask icons --check`: 0 breaches.\n- Quick gate (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` + clippy): green, 7 new\n  tests.\n\n## Not exercised here\n\n- The browser open itself: the tests assert the `OpenUrl` platform-output\n  command, not the browser. Hand GUI test by the maintainer before merge.\n- Clipboard paste into GitHub: manual check in the same GUI test.\n\nNote for the reviewer: this PR touches `.github/`, so `pr-test.yml` refuses\nit and the review builds locally (read, not built: the yellow\n`needs-maintainer` path).\n\nfork synced at v0.20.0 (branch off origin/main 2aca3e55).\n\nChangelog: The status strip gained a Report door: it opens a prefilled GitHub issue and copies a document screenshot to the clipboard (#1696, PR #1798)\n\nFixes #1696\n",
